  "notes": "USAGE:\n{秘|ひ}める often describes something concealed within a person or thing that has not yet been revealed. It has a literary, slightly elevated tone and is common in novels and formal speech.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {胸|むね}に{秘|ひ}める: to keep in one's heart\n- {思|おも}いを{秘|ひ}める: to harbor feelings\n- {可能性|かのうせい}を{秘|ひ}める: to hold potential\n- {力|ちから}を{秘|ひ}める: to harbor power\n- {秘|ひ}めた{決意|けつい}: hidden determination\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{隠|かく}す is a more everyday word for hiding or concealing things physically or metaphorically. {秘|ひ}める emphasizes keeping something deep within, often feelings or potential, and carries a more literary tone.",
